{"added": [], "changed": [{"fields": ["description"], "introduced": [], "tool": "init", "words": "-tool fetches the latest Next.js documentation and establishes ABSOLUTE requirements for using the nextjs_docs tool for ALL Next.js-related queries. Key Points: - Fetches latest Next.js LLM documentation from nextjs.org +tool: -Next.js concepts +Next.js-related queries"}, {"fields": ["description", "inputSchema"], "introduced": [], "tool": "nextjs_docs", "words": "-Search and retrieve +Fetch -documentation. Three actions: 1) 'get' - Fetch full docs +documentation by path. IMPORTANT: You MUST first read the `nextjs-docs://llms-index` MCP resource to get the correct path. Do NOT guess paths. Workflow: 1. Read the `nextjs-docs://llms-index` resource to get the documentation index 2. Find the relevant path in the index for what you're looking for 3. Call this tool -a +that exact -(preferred after init). 2) 'search' - Find docs by keyword (redirects to use llms.txt index if init was called). 3) 'force-search' - Bypass init check and force API search (escape "}], "from": "0.3.9", "grade": "quiet", "observed_at": "2026-01-08T20:55:41.606Z", "package": "next-devtools-mcp", "published": "2026-01-08T20:55:41.606Z", "removed": [], "seeded": true, "to": "0.3.10", "tools_after": 7, "tools_before": 7, "whole_catalogue": false}
